/: 034: Graphiti Oscillation as Market Failure — NormCode Analysis Plan
/: Phase 1: Feed oscillation trace from experiment
/: Phase 2: Lift to formal model (EMLTree anti-coherent pair)
/: Phase 3: Ground the fix as a NormCode norm (prefer_current rule)
/: Phase 4: Verify closure fixed point with and without tie-breaking

concept community_7, community_9, pivot_node_C, tie_condition
concept oscillation_state, stable_state, closure_outcome
concept iter_count, vote_tally_7, vote_tally_9
concept deg_s2ville, deg_s3ville, symmetric_deg_condition
concept type_lattice_graph, adjacency_edge, edge_weight
concept converged_norm, oscillating_norm, certificate

/: Data structures for the per-iteration trace -:/
concept iteration_assignments    /: Map node→community per iteration -:/
concept vote_history             /: Record of vote tallies at C per iteration -:/
concept tie_break_rule           /: "prefer current" or "prefer higher" -:/

/: Relations -:/

relation build_entity_graph : type_lattice_graph -> adjacency_edge
    /: From the 11 types and 5 adjacencies -:/

relation measure_neighbor_votes : adjacency_edge -> vote_tally_7 × vote_tally_9
    /: For each node, count edge_weight to comm 7 vs comm 9 -:/

relation detect_symmetric_tie : vote_tally_7 × vote_tally_9 -> tie_condition
    /: True when vote_tally_7 = vote_tally_9 -:/

relation iterate_no_break : adjacency_edge × tie_break_rule -> oscillation_state
    /: Without prefer_current: infinite oscillation -:/

relation iterate_with_break : adjacency_edge × tie_break_rule -> stable_state
    /: With prefer_current: converges in ≤ |V| steps -:/

relation closure_on_oscillation : oscillation_state -> oscillating_norm
    /: closure() on oscillating trace has no fixed point -:/

relation closure_on_convergent : stable_state -> converged_norm
    /: closure() on convergent trace has fixed point -:/

relation certify_stable : converged_norm -> certificate
    /: Emit CortexCertificate for stable outcome -:/

relation connect_to_dolly_zoom : symmetric_deg_condition -> deg_s2ville × deg_s3ville
    /: deg(C)_S₂ville = deg(C)_S₃ville  iff  [s₂⁺(i), s₃⁺(j)] = 0 -:/

/: 
Path A: No tie-breaking — infinite oscillation
  Shows that the upstream algorithm never converges.
  closure_is_fixed_point = false.
:/
path: oscillation_without_fix(type_lattice_graph, tie_break_rule) -> oscilating_norm
    <= build_entity_graph(type_lattice_graph)
    <- adjacency_edge
    <= measure_neighbor_votes(adjacency_edge)
    <- vote_tally_7
    <- vote_tally_9
    <= detect_symmetric_tie(vote_tally_7, vote_tally_9)
    <- tie_condition
    <= iterate_no_break(adjacency_edge, tie_break_rule)
    <- oscillation_state
    <= closure_on_oscillation(oscillation_state)
    <* self_check_norm(oscillating_norm)
    :closure:

/: 
Path B: With tie-breaking — converges to stable state
  Prefer_current breaks the symmetry.
  closure_is_fixed_point = true.
:/
path: convergence_with_fix(type_lattice_graph, tie_break_rule) -> certificate
    <= build_entity_graph(type_lattice_graph)
    <- adjacency_edge
    <= measure_neighbor_votes(adjacency_edge)
    <- vote_tally_7
    <- vote_tally_9
    <= iterate_with_break(adjacency_edge, tie_break_rule)
    <- stable_state
    <= closure_on_convergent(stable_state)
    <- converged_norm
    <= certify_stable(converged_norm)
    <- certificate
    :closure:

/: 
Path C: Lift to Lean formal layer
  Connect the concrete oscillation to the commutator vanishing theorem.
:/
path: lift_to_lean(type_lattice_graph, pivot_node_C) -> deg_s2ville × deg_s3ville
    <= build_entity_graph(type_lattice_graph)
    <- adjacency_edge
    <= connect_to_dolly_zoom(symmetric_deg_condition)
    <- deg_s2ville
    <- deg_s3ville

/: 
Observable: when deg_s2ville = deg_s3ville, the oscillation is structurally
necessary — no tie-breaking rule can make the market converge without
changing the underlying graph topology.
:/
